_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.06268211408517665,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.050962554051299014,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.10425929693024517,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01219,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Simmons First National Corporation operates as the bank holding company for Simmons Bank that provides banking and other financial products and services to individuals and businesses. The company offers deposits, checking, and savings accounts; loan products, such as consumer, real estate, commercial, agricultural, equipment, warehouse lending, and SBA lending; specialized products and services, including credit cards, trust and fiduciary services, investments, and insurance; and treasury management services. It also provides ATM services; internet and mobile banking platforms; overdraft facilities; safe deposit boxes; and brokerage services. The company has operations in Arkansas, Kansas, Missouri, Oklahoma, Tennessee, and Texas. Simmons First National Corporation was founded in 1903 and is headquartered in Pine Bluff, Arkansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James M. Brogdon CPA | President, CEO & Non-Independent Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $38K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $152K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 59\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Simmons First National Corporat is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.4B market cap on $103M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -51% over the past three years and -12% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","The business throws off $411M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 398 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss.","Net dilution runs at 6.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 10% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.04892546867855572},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 86/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 64% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(SFNC) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/SFNC_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111326010402_1794593042.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794593042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Survey: Simmons First National (NASDAQ:SFNC) and Summit State Bank (NASDAQ:SSBI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/financial-survey-simmons-first-national-nasdaqsfnc-and-summit-state-bank-nasdaqssbi.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793801705.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(SFNC) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/SFNC_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry